        "slide": 1,
        "role": "cover",
        "subject": "A kit crossover seen head on at night behind a white stop bar. Two emissive lamp strips sit on the nose, and two warm spot lobes fall from the lower fascia onto continental crosswalk bars that run off the bottom edge toward the reader. A worn centre dash line recedes into a dark terracotta haze.",
        "visual_consequence": "Without the headline, a car with its lamps on waits at painted crossing markings on a public road after dark, the place Proposition A governs. No camera is shown. The lit paint is the subject, which sets up the deck's road-paint vocabulary.",
        "weakness": "Same as the earlier reading. The plate reads as a muted grey and blue panel, lower in value than the lamp strips and the lit bars. The fill puts two soft hot spots on the fascia. The stop bar's shadowed half has a cold top face. The upper body and glass are simple dark planes, rounded enough that the car does not read as boxes.",
